    "q-176872": {
      "dom_id": "step-q176872",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬[¬(¬(¬C)∧D)].$",
      "worked_solution": "Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So, we can simplify $¬(¬C)$ to $C.$ \n\nAs a result of this, the statement simplifes to \n\n$$\n¬[¬(C∧D)].\n$$\n\nThen, we can simplify $¬[¬(C∧D)]]$ to $C∧D.$\n\nTherefore, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\nC∧D.\n$$",
