    "q-182356": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182356",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∨B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we add a column for $¬A,$ where the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the column for $A.$ \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,¬A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $¬A∨B.$ Remember that $¬A∨B$ is true if either $¬A$ is true or $B$ is true. \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,¬A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∨B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
